**LOAN AGREEMENT**

**January 14, 2021**

**BETWEEN:**

**ABC Financial Inc.,** a Delaware corporation with its principal place of business at 123 Main Street, Anytown, USA 12345 (hereinafter "Lender"),

**AND:**

**XYZ Corporation,** a Delaware corporation with its principal place of business at 456 Elm Street, Anytown, USA 67890,

**XYZ Subsidiary Ltd.**, an Irish limited company with its principal place of business at 789 Oak Avenue, Dublin, Ireland, D01 F01 (hereinafter collectively referred to as "Borrowers").

**WHEREAS,** Lender desires to make loans to Borrowers and Borrowers are desirous of receiving such loans on the terms and conditions set forth herein;

**NOW, THEREFORE,** in consideration of the mutual covenants and agreements contained herein, the parties hereto agree as follows:

**1. Loan Terms**

1.1 Lender shall make loans to Borrowers in the aggregate principal amount of One Hundred Million United States Dollars ($100,000,000) (the "Loan Amount").

1.2 The Loan Amount shall be divided into two separate loans, with the first loan amounting to Seventy-Five Million United States Dollars ($75,000,000) (the "First Loan") and the second loan amounting to Twenty-Five Million United States Dollars ($25,000,000) (the "Second Loan").

1.3 The Loan Amount shall be evidenced by one or more promissory notes executed by Borrowers (the "Notes").

**2. Interest and Fees**

2.1 Borrowers shall pay interest on the outstanding principal balance of each Loan at the rate of 4.5% per annum, payable semi-annually in arrears.

2.2 Borrowers shall pay a commitment fee of 0.5% per annum on the undrawn portion of the Loan Amount.

2.3 The first interest payment shall be due on July 14, 2021, and subsequent interest payments shall be due on the same date each six months thereafter.

**3. Default and Remedies**

3.1 In the event of any default under this Agreement or any of the Notes, Lender shall have the right to declare all or any portion of the outstanding principal and accrued but unpaid interest immediately due and payable.

3.2 In the event of any such default, Lender may exercise any remedies available to it at law or in equity, including without limitation, foreclosure, repossession, and the sale of any collateral pledged by Borrowers.

**4. Representations and Warranties**

Borrowers represent and warrant to Lender that:

4.1 They have the full power and authority to execute, deliver, and perform their obligations under this Agreement and the Notes.

4.2 The execution, delivery, and performance of this Agreement and the Notes have been duly authorized by all necessary corporate action on the part of Borrowers.

4.3 This Agreement constitutes the valid and binding obligation of Borrowers, enforceable in accordance with its terms, except as limited by bankruptcy, insolvency, or other laws of general applicability relating to or affecting the enforcement of creditors' rights.

**5. Governing Law**

This Agreement shall be governed by and construed in accordance with the laws of the State of Delaware, without giving effect to its conflict of laws provisions.

**6. Counterparts**

This Agreement may be executed in counterparts, each of which shall be deemed an original, but all of which together shall constitute one and the same instrument.

**7. Entire Agreement**

This Agreement contains the entire agreement between the parties hereto with respect to the subject matter hereof and supersedes all prior and contemporaneous agreements and understandings, whether written or oral, relating to the same subject matter.

**8. Amendments**

This Agreement may not be amended or modified except by a written instrument executed by both parties.

**IN WITNESS WHEREOF,** the parties have executed this Agreement as of the date first written above.

